# Generated artifacts: parquet caches, model checkpoints, MLflow runs, SFT trajectories.
# Everything the pipeline produces lives here so the `data/` *package* never collides with
# cached *data files*.
artifacts/*

# ...except the agent trajectories. They are a RESULT, not a cache: 767 grounded
# transcripts generated against a local Ollama model, which Colab cannot reproduce because
# it has no Ollama. Ignoring them meant a fresh clone could never run the SFT cell, and the
# notebook asked people to upload a file by hand. 5.7MB is a reasonable price for making
# the run self-contained and the dataset versioned alongside the code that consumed it.
!artifacts/trajectories/
artifacts/trajectories/*
!artifacts/trajectories/*.jsonl

# Environments
.venv/

# uv.lock IS committed, deliberately. This is an application, not a library, and the
# dissertation claims reproducible results -- an exact dependency resolution is part of
# that claim. requirements.txt is the same snapshot for readers without uv.

# Secrets
.env

# MLflow (if ever run outside artifacts/)
mlruns/
mlartifacts/

# Data files
*.parquet
*.feather
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Model weights
*.pt
*.pth
*.safetensors
*.ckpt

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Per-fold backtest checkpoints (resumable; regenerated on demand)
artifacts/results/_folds_*.csv
